        <h2 class="section-title">Research Interests</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="research-content reveal">
        <ul class="research-list">
          <li class="research-item">
            <div class="research-item-heading">
              <span class="research-index" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
              <h3 class="research-item-title">Reliable LLM Agents and Failure Diagnosis</h3>
            </div>
            <div class="research-item-body">
              <p class="research-item-text">
                I study how LLM agents fail across multi-turn interaction, input faults, and cooperative settings,
                how those failures can be diagnosed, and how execution experience can make agent harnesses more adaptive.
              </p>
              <div class="research-citations">
                <span class="research-works-label">Selected works</span>
                <span class="research-works-list">
                  <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.14159" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="research-citation-link">MemoHarness <span class="research-venue">arXiv'26</span></a>
                  <span class="research-work-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
                  <span class="research-citation">Drift-Bench <span class="research-venue">ICML'26</span></span>
                  <span class="research-work-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
                  <a href="https://dl.acm.org/doi/abs/10.1145/3774905.3793130" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="research-citation-link">IntraAI <span class="research-venue">WWW'26 Demo</span></a>
                </span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="research-item">
            <div class="research-item-heading">
              <span class="research-index" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
              <h3 class="research-item-title">Alignment under Training and Deployment Shifts</h3>
            </div>
            <div class="research-item-body">
              <p class="research-item-text">
                I investigate how alignment risks emerge as models acquire new capabilities or move into constrained
                deployment environments, together with guardian and advisor mechanisms for safer behavior.
              </p>
              <div class="research-citations">
                <span class="research-works-label">Selected works</span>
                <span class="research-works-list">
                  <span class="research-citation">Capability-Oriented Training Induced Alignment Risk <span class="research-venue">ICML'26</span></span>
                  <span class="research-work-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
                  <a href="https://2026.aclweb.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="research-citation-link">Guardian-as-an-Advisor <span class="research-venue">ACL'26 Findings</span></a>
                  <span class="research-work-sep" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
                  <a href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/2602.20042" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="research-citation-link">AI Alignment Breaks at the Edge <span class="research-venue">Position Paper</span></a>
                </span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </li>
